  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nRisk-on rally brewing as futures surge on Iran peace deal momentum. SPY pushing +1.9% with tech leading the charge at +3.66%, while VIX drops 6.2% to 22.7 signaling reduced fear premium. Energy getting hammered down 2.8% as oil geopolitical risk unwinds.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Fox-Roku Deal</strong> - $22B acquisition sending ripples through streaming/media space, watch XLC momentum</li>\n<li><strong>Iran Peace Progress</strong> - Hormuz strait normalization by August could crater oil further, pressure XLE names</li>\n<li><strong>DOMO Earnings</strong> - After market close, EPS est -0.0673, key SaaS sentiment gauge</li>\n<li><strong>Consumer Bank Rotation</strong> - CNBC highlighting lower oil beneficiaries, watch regional bank plays</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>Iran deal removes major geopolitical overhang while STOXX 600 hits records, suggesting global risk appetite returning. Lower energy costs boost consumer spending power into summer.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nClear flight to growth as tech explodes +3.66% while defensive sectors lag. Energy's -2.83% decline creates opportunity if Iran talks stall, but momentum favors continued rotation into consumer discretionary and industrials. Healthcare weakness at -0.42% suggests profit-taking from recent strength.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>Watch oil futures at open - sub-$70 WTI could accelerate energy sector washout while boosting airline and transportation names.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY 760</strong> - Resistance level from May highs, break triggers momentum algos</li>\n<li><strong>QQQ 750</strong> - Round number magnet, watch for profit-taking if we gap above</li>\n<li><strong>XLE 85</strong> - Critical support for energy ETF, break could see 80 fast</li>\n<li><strong>VIX 20</strong> - Sub-20 print would signal full complacency mode</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Iran deal optimism could be premature - any headline reversal sends oil spiking and crushes this momentum trade. VIX still elevated above 20 suggesting underlying caution.</div>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>",
